:'''Enraged Oronyx Devotee:''' I want to vote! Tell me how I can vote!
:'''Rational Talanton Devotee:''' Take your ceramic shard engraved with the {{Rubi|Kephale|Worldbearing Titan}} rune, select the Council of Elders in your heart, and pray silently until the shard registers your choice. Then toss it into the dolium.
:'''Enraged Oronyx Devotee:''' The Council of Elders? More like the council of buffoons! The black tide took my hometown long ago! Who are they kidding with bringing back Era Chrysea? It's all a sham to create their own Era Chrysea in Okhema!
:'''Rational Talanton Devotee:''' The Titans are just... So long as we do not overstep our bounds again, we will not incur divine wrath.
:'''Enraged Oronyx Devotee:''' Oh, please. The time when these deranged Titans should have vacated their spot to the demigods is long overdue! You'll see soon enough, you old fogey!
:'''Rational Talanton Devotee:''' And I pray that {{Rubi|Talanton|Law Titan}} smacks some sense into you with their scales. We shall see how this turns out!
:'''Castorice:''' That was... quite a spectacle.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Just another peaceful day in Okhema.
::'''Castorice:''' ...I suppose "peaceful" is technically correct if no actual violence happened...
::Yeah, watching people squabble is kind of fun.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Yeah, watching people squabble is kind of fun.
:'''Castorice:''' Hm? You're interested in that? Well, you'll feel right at home in Okhema then.
:'''Castorice:''' To this day, I still find it almost unreal that Okhema is the only place illuminated by light amidst the crumbling ruins of Amphoreus, and its people are even holding votes to reconcile differing opinions...
:'''Castorice:''' This peaceful sight is making me forget that this is the end times.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} This is what the Flame-Chase Journey is all about.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Shouldn't you have gotten used to it by now?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} ...You look very confused.
:'''Castorice:''' ...
:'''Castorice:''' Before coming here, I had lived for many years in Aidonia, a city of rime and frost. The people there were devotees of {{Rubi|Thanatos|Death Titan}}, and were well-known for their unique burial rites and traditions.
:'''Castorice:''' ...Traditions that I played a major role in.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Because of the curse on you?
:'''Castorice:''' Yes. You now know me as the mortician of Okhema...
:'''Castorice:''' But back in those days, I was Aidonia's Maiden of War.
:'''Castorice:''' I was trudging across the frosty plains on my own when the Aidonians found me. They saw the curse in me as a blessing from {{Rubi|Thanatos|Death Titan}}, and believed that my hands could correct the Era Chrysea's mistake and lead them to meet the great god of death.
:'''Castorice:''' They provided me shelter, but in return...
:'''Castorice:''' I was expected to grant "merciful deaths" to war captives, prisoners bound for execution, and heroes alike.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Is that some sort of end-of-life care?
::'''Castorice:''' Is that how you see it too? But...
::Isn't that just an executioner?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Isn't that just an executioner?
:'''Castorice:''' Yes...
:'''Castorice:''' No matter how kind or cruel the means, nothing can change the essence of death...
:{{tx}}

